      "message": "That\u0027s what I tried originally, and it made bazel unhappy (which is why I was passing around pointer + size). SkSpan_impl.h is part of base, whereas SkSpan.h is part of core. That impacts which other TUs (and headers) are allowed to include it. Various things that transitively include this (including SkRasterPipeline_opts.h) aren\u0027t configured to see core headers. Interestingly, it looks like we must have hit this already (or just did this for other reasons), as there are ~25 existing includes of SkSpan_impl.h",
      "parentUuid": "07a20dd1_e09674d6",
      "range": {
